### Anything else?

One related thing in Safari that the fix doesn't cover: when a guard rejects synchronously after a plain link click or the back button, `cancel()` runs while the `navigate` event is still being dispatched. At that point the URL hasn't changed yet, so there's nothing to roll back, but the browser commits the intercepted navigation right after. The URL ends up on the rejected route while the router stays on the previous page. That's a different code path, so I left it out.
